HST Office: ribbon groups at their medium and small size form Office's even 3-row grid; large labels wrap.

1.0.2 ribbon (owner decisions 14/11/2026, gap list G01-G03, G09): a group keeps its labels as long as possible.
At the medium size the buttons of a large toolbox become small icons with their label on the right in even
columns of three rows (24 logical px, 2 px apart), filled top to bottom then left to right; at the small size
the same grid without labels. Every item starts at its column's left edge, so the icons line up and nothing
is staggered. A large button's label wider than 62 logical px wraps at its most balanced space (at most two
lines), and a large menu button is split as in Office: the image runs the command, the label below it opens
the menu, with ▾ after the label's last line instead of a column of its own on the right.

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonGrid.hxx: the grid geometry and stackGroup (plain arithmetic, unit tested); LABEL_WRAP.
- HstRibbonLadder.cxx stackLargeButtons: the ribbon's large buttons are one toolbox each, so at the medium and
  small size consecutive ones are re-attached in their group's grid in columns of three (the caption moves
  below the third row; separators and buttons that stay large span the extra row); the large size restores
  the authored attachments. A toolbox of several buttons uses ToolBox::HstSetGridRows instead.
- ToolBox::HstSetGridRows (opt-in, ribbon ladder only); ImplCalcSize and ImplFormat lay out the grid.
- toolbox.cxx: balanced label wrap for ribbon toolboxes, split large menu buttons (ImplToolItem::GetDropDownRect
  returns the label part); HstRibbonLadder.cxx: grid rows 3 at the medium and small size of large toolboxes.

