+// HST Office: the even grid of a ribbon group at its medium and small size (Office's 3-row columns).
+// Plain integer arithmetic without LibreOffice types, so it can be unit tested on its own
+// (tests/unit/test_ribbon_grid.py compiles it from the patch with a test driver).
+//
+// The items of one toolbox fill columns top to bottom, `rows` items per column, left to right; a separator
+// ends the current column and stands as a thin column of its own. Every row has the same height and every
+// item starts at its column's left edge, so the icons line up in even columns and rows (never staggered).
+// A column is as wide as its widest item; the grid is as high as `rows` rows whatever the item count.
+
